<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila call rate up as banks square positions.</title>
<headline>Manila call rate up as banks square positions.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------------- Oct 2 ----------------------------</p>
<p>* Liquidity seen easing next week</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Manila overnight money rose for the third consecutive day on Wednesday as more banks sought pesos to square their positions before the weekend, traders said.</p>
<p>The average interbank call loan rate rose to 12.46875 from 12.15625.</p>
<p>&quot;More banks were trying square to off their reserve positions. They didn't borrow at the start of the week, hoping interest rates will go down,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
</text>
